thank you, MADAM Clerk.

01:08:17.498 --> 01:08:21.980
Colleagues, I would ask that we

01:08:21.269 --> 01:08:22.300
conclude today's board meeting

01:08:22.300 --> 01:08:25.390
with an in memoriam for the

01:08:25.390 --> 01:08:25.706
late alisha miele who is the

01:08:25.706 --> 01:08:28.576
father of mosher miele, a

01:08:28.576 --> 01:08:29.410
veteran deputy city attorney

01:08:29.410 --> 01:08:30.440
and a friend of colleague and

01:08:30.440 --> 01:08:32.180
colleague of mine and a

01:08:32.180 --> 01:08:32.980
longtime community leader.

01:08:32.980 --> 01:08:33.314
Alijah miele was born in jordan

01:08:33.314 --> 01:08:35.314
in 1932.

01:08:36.684 --> 01:08:37.352
He immigrated to san francisco

01:08:37.352 --> 01:08:40.352
in 1966 in pursuit of the

01:08:40.622 --> 01:08:41.256
american dream a dream he would

01:08:41.256 --> 01:08:43.656
fulfill with hard work,

01:08:43.725 --> 01:08:44.459
resilience and boundless love

01:08:44.459 --> 01:08:44.793
for his adopted country and his

01:08:44.793 --> 01:08:46.793
family.

01:08:47.362 --> 01:08:48.960
Prior to immigrating to the

01:08:48.960 --> 01:08:50.965
united states, he was a skilled

01:08:50.965 --> 01:08:51.732
carpenter even contributing to

01:08:51.732 --> 01:08:54.732
the production of lawrence of

01:08:54.970 --> 01:08:55.837
arabia part of a production

01:08:55.837 --> 01:08:58.907
design team that would go on to

01:08:58.907 --> 01:08:59.641
win the 1963 oscar for best art

01:08:59.641 --> 01:09:00.375
direction and set design which

01:09:00.375 --> 01:09:03.178
was one of seven oscars that

01:09:03.178 --> 01:09:03.612
film won that year including

01:09:03.612 --> 01:09:04.279
best picture.

01:09:04.279 --> 01:09:07.279
Here in san francisco, ali

01:09:07.548 --> 01:09:08.249
worked as a busser at original

01:09:08.249 --> 01:09:11.249
joe's on taylor street and

01:09:11.319 --> 01:09:11.819
became a proud member of the

01:09:11.819 --> 01:09:12.554
carpenters union.

01:09:12.554 --> 01:09:14.656
He later moved to los angeles

01:09:14.656 --> 01:09:15.324
where he met the love of his

01:09:15.324 --> 01:09:15.958
life antoinette jameel and

01:09:15.958 --> 01:09:18.358
built a successful small

01:09:18.894 --> 01:09:19.261
business the monte carlo

01:09:19.261 --> 01:09:19.995
limousine.

01:09:19.995 --> 01:09:22.931
He was beloved by his clients

01:09:22.931 --> 01:09:23.565
including boxing legend

01:09:23.565 --> 01:09:25.934
muhammad ali who famously

01:09:25.934 --> 01:09:26.534
insisted on sitting up front to

01:09:26.534 --> 01:09:28.934
swap stories with him.

01:09:29.939 --> 01:09:30.706
Ali eventually retired back

01:09:30.706 --> 01:09:31.373
in the bay area living in the

01:09:31.373 --> 01:09:33.373
salvation army silvercrest

01:09:33.642 --> 01:09:34.376
apartments in south of market

01:09:34.376 --> 01:09:34.910
and also in willow grill at

01:09:34.910 --> 01:09:37.310
glen in san jose.

01:09:38.280 --> 01:09:39.140
He was a devoted husband,

01:09:39.140 --> 01:09:41.414
father and grandfather survived

01:09:41.416 --> 01:09:42.151
by the love of his life and his

01:09:42.151 --> 01:09:45.151
partner antoinette and his son

01:09:45.320 --> 01:09:45.620
mo and grandchildren oliver and

01:09:45.620 --> 01:09:46.387
kate.

01:09:46.387 --> 01:09:48.424
Our hearts go out to them and

01:09:48.424 --> 01:09:49.910
to all who join us and all are

01:09:49.910 --> 01:09:52.910
in honoring ali's legacy a

01:09:53.280 --> 01:09:53.696
well-lived life rooted in hard

01:09:53.696 --> 01:09:54.429
work, community and family.

01:09:54.429 --> 01:09:56.765
MAY he rest in peace and the

01:09:56.765 --> 01:09:57.199
rest I submit.

01:09:57.199 --> 01:09:57.900
>> thank you.

01:09:57.900 --> 01:09:59.900
Supervisor dorsey supervisor

01:10:00.803 --> 01:10:01.269
and gaudio submit.

01:10:01.269 --> 01:10:03.269
>> thank you.

01:10:04.272 --> 01:10:04.941
Supervisor fielder.

01:10:04.941 --> 01:10:07.341
>> thank you, MADAM Clerk.

01:10:08.511 --> 01:10:09.245
Colleagues today I have found

01:10:09.245 --> 01:10:12.245
it imperative to introduce a

01:10:12.815 --> 01:10:13.516
resolution addressing the

01:10:13.516 --> 01:10:15.916
increasing crisis of family

01:10:17.190 --> 01:10:19.155
homelessness and the harm on

01:10:19.155 --> 01:10:19.588
children from the reinstated 90

01:10:19.588 --> 01:10:20.255
day shelter.

01:10:20.255 --> 01:10:22.655
>> length of stay policy.

01:10:23.426 --> 01:10:24.127
For the past few weeks I've

01:10:24.127 --> 01:10:27.127
heard more and more stories

01:10:27.197 --> 01:10:27.797
from families with looming

01:10:27.797 --> 01:10:30.197
eviction dates at their

01:10:30.900 --> 01:10:31.567
shelters who are fearful and

01:10:31.567 --> 01:10:32.301
stress about the threat of

01:10:32.301 --> 01:10:35.237
eviction and being returned to

01:10:35.237 --> 01:10:36.105
the streets.

01:10:36.105 --> 01:10:38.574
>> we we've been told by two

01:10:38.574 --> 01:10:39.342
sage and the mayor's office

01:10:39.342 --> 01:10:40.760
that this policy is to better

01:10:40.760 --> 01:10:43.760
address the needs of families

01:10:43.446 --> 01:10:44.800
in our community and to ensure

01:10:44.800 --> 01:10:46.480
families are making quote

01:10:47.217 --> 01:10:47.817
positive progress on their

01:10:47.817 --> 01:10:49.817
families success plans.

01:10:50.920 --> 01:10:51.654
>> however, the actual

01:10:51.654 --> 01:10:54.540
implementation of this policy

01:10:54.724 --> 01:10:55.458
has been a nightmare for

01:10:55.458 --> 01:10:56.920
families and fails to solve for

01:10:56.920 --> 01:10:58.492
larger barriers that are

01:10:59.290 --> 01:10:59.663
actually in the way of families

01:10:59.663 --> 01:11:01.663
making positive progress.

01:11:02.999 --> 01:11:05.769
The policy has escalated to the

01:11:05.769 --> 01:11:06.469
point that just yesterday two

01:11:06.469 --> 01:11:09.272
families were facing 5 P.M.

01:11:09.272 --> 01:11:10.390
Evictions with the threat of

01:11:10.390 --> 01:11:13.390
the shelter provider calling as

01:11:13.176 --> 01:11:16.176
of today to remove them.

01:11:16.447 --> 01:11:17.281
I repeat a shelter provider

01:11:17.281 --> 01:11:20.281
threatened to call police on

01:11:20.484 --> 01:11:21.218
families at a shelter.

01:11:21.218 --> 01:11:23.753
>> it turns out that the

01:11:23.753 --> 01:11:24.421
families were waiting for

01:11:24.421 --> 01:11:25.122
scheduled appointments for

01:11:25.122 --> 01:11:27.122
housing referrals something

01:11:28.291 --> 01:11:28.992
that should have been

01:11:28.992 --> 01:11:30.992
considered positive progress.

01:11:31.761 --> 01:11:32.496
>> agency overturned the

01:11:32.496 --> 01:11:34.732
provider's removal decision and

01:11:34.732 --> 01:11:35.432
the families received 30 day

01:11:35.432 --> 01:11:38.432
extensions which is a relief

01:11:39.690 --> 01:11:39.770
but is only going to bring us

01:11:39.770 --> 01:11:42.806
back to square one in APRIL.

01:11:42.806 --> 01:11:43.506
>> these are not anomalies as

01:11:43.506 --> 01:11:46.506
of this policy rollout I've

01:11:46.610 --> 01:11:47.310
heard from as of used social

01:11:47.310 --> 01:11:49.310
workers, medical professionals

01:11:51.215 --> 01:11:51.983
and community organizations.

01:11:51.983 --> 01:11:54.618
Dozens of stories of confusion

01:11:54.618 --> 01:11:55.386
and fear.

01:11:55.386 --> 01:11:57.786
>> and this reinstated policy

01:11:58.956 --> 01:11:59.723
in its current implementation

01:11:59.723 --> 01:12:00.570
and is ineffective as it is

01:12:00.570 --> 01:12:02.570
callous.

01:12:03.126 --> 01:12:03.827
I outlined in an extensive memo

01:12:03.827 --> 01:12:06.227
last week the implementation

01:12:06.597 --> 01:12:07.298
issues in this shelter state

01:12:07.298 --> 01:12:10.298
policy such as families not

01:12:10.401 --> 01:12:11.680
being informed of their ability

01:12:11.680 --> 01:12:13.468
to request an extension.

01:12:14.405 --> 01:12:15.106
The incredible discretion

01:12:15.106 --> 01:12:15.873
providers and case managers

01:12:15.873 --> 01:12:18.873
have in dictating what positive

01:12:18.942 --> 01:12:19.677
progress means let alone the

01:12:19.677 --> 01:12:22.770
larger systemic barriers that

01:12:22.746 --> 01:12:23.514
families have in accessing

01:12:23.514 --> 01:12:23.847
housing and exiting the shelter

01:12:23.847 --> 01:12:25.847
system.

01:12:26.551 --> 01:12:27.252
>> even hsa and shelter

01:12:27.252 --> 01:12:29.252
providers have acknowledged

01:12:30.221 --> 01:12:30.922
those barriers.

01:12:30.922 --> 01:12:31.656
Also most families are not

01:12:31.656 --> 01:12:34.910
being informed of their right

01:12:34.910 --> 01:12:34.926
to submit a grievance should an

01:12:34.926 --> 01:12:37.928
extension be denied which is a

01:12:37.928 --> 01:12:40.328
violation of city policy.

01:12:41.565 --> 01:12:42.267
>> I sent this memo to the

01:12:42.267 --> 01:12:45.267
mayor's policy chief and hsa

01:12:45.370 --> 01:12:45.971
and they have been open to

01:12:45.971 --> 01:12:47.971
working on solutions.

01:12:48.873 --> 01:12:49.641
I'm now formally calling on the

01:12:49.641 --> 01:12:52.877
mayor and agency to rescind or

01:12:52.877 --> 01:12:53.611
drastically reform the 90 day

01:12:53.611 --> 01:12:56.611
shelter, stay policy and work

01:12:56.881 --> 01:12:57.615
with the board of supervisors

01:12:57.615 --> 01:12:58.282
and stakeholders to develop a

01:12:58.282 --> 01:13:00.682
policy that avoids placing

01:13:01.486 --> 01:13:02.187
undue stress on families.

01:13:02.187 --> 01:13:04.587
These reforms should include

01:13:05.323 --> 01:13:05.990
increases in shelter and

01:13:05.990 --> 01:13:08.390
housing options to address

01:13:08.727 --> 01:13:09.427
family homelessness.

01:13:09.427 --> 01:13:11.827
>> this policy is partially

01:13:12.764 --> 01:13:13.431
predicated on the notion that

01:13:13.431 --> 01:13:15.831
families refusing to leave

01:13:16.667 --> 01:13:17.436
shelters are the problem.

01:13:17.436 --> 01:13:20.105
>> there has been no readily

01:13:20.105 --> 01:13:20.339
available data to suggest this

01:13:20.339 --> 01:13:21.106
.

01:13:21.106 --> 01:13:23.708
No parent wishes to raise their

01:13:23.708 --> 01:13:24.376
children in a shelter.

01:13:24.376 --> 01:13:27.376
These shelters are a last

01:13:27.612 --> 01:13:28.480
resort for families.

01:13:28.480 --> 01:13:29.800
This policy is not working and

01:13:29.800 --> 01:13:31.800
rather than committing

01:13:32.500 --> 01:13:32.784
substantial jail time in all of

01:13:32.784 --> 01:13:35.184
the different branches of

01:13:35.988 --> 01:13:38.988
litigating family cases one by

01:13:39.158 --> 01:13:39.925
one we need a better policy.

01:13:39.925 --> 01:13:42.925
>> the stories we are hearing

01:13:43.362 --> 01:13:44.290
are heart wrenching and I

01:13:44.290 --> 01:13:44.329
literally cannot sleep at

01:13:44.329 --> 01:13:44.963
night.

01:13:44.963 --> 01:13:46.963
>> knowing families with

01:13:47.732 --> 01:13:48.467
children of all ages are being

01:13:48.467 --> 01:13:51.467
subject to this policy with

01:13:51.937 --> 01:13:52.738
inconsistency and callousness.

01:13:52.738 --> 01:13:55.441
>> no child should have to live

01:13:55.441 --> 01:13:56.175
on the streets and the city

01:13:56.175 --> 01:13:58.877
shouldn't be the cause for any

01:13:58.877 --> 01:13:59.111
child being back on the streets

01:13:59.111 --> 01:14:01.111
.

01:14:02.547 --> 01:14:03.315
As the policy currently stands

01:14:03.315 --> 01:14:06.184
,we need to do better.

01:14:06.184 --> 01:14:06.919
>> we can end family

01:14:06.919 --> 01:14:07.586
homelessness in san francisco

01:14:07.586 --> 01:14:10.123
and we should be working

01:14:10.123 --> 01:14:10.556
together to make it happen.

01:14:10.556 --> 01:14:12.556
>> thank you.

01:14:13.926 --> 01:14:14.493
Supervisors chen melgar and

01:14:14.493 --> 01:14:16.893
walton for your early

01:14:16.996 --> 01:14:17.229
co-sponsorship and partnership

01:14:17.229 --> 01:14:18.197
.

01:14:18.197 --> 01:14:18.731
>> I hope all of you will join

01:14:18.731 --> 01:14:21.131
us in supporting san

01:14:21.667 --> 01:14:22.368
francisco's most vulnerable

01:14:22.368 --> 01:14:25.270
children and working to find

01:14:25.270 --> 01:14:25.804
real lasting solutions to

01:14:25.804 --> 01:14:26.338
family homelessness.

01:14:26.338 --> 01:14:26.738
The rest I submit.

01:14:26.738 --> 01:14:28.738
Thank you.

01:14:29.409 --> 01:14:31.409
Supervisor fielder.

01:14:33.246 --> 01:14:33.712
Supervisor mohamud submit.

01:14:33.712 --> 01:14:34.447
>> thank you.

01:14:34.447 --> 01:14:36.847
Supervisor gentleman thank you,

01:14:37.183 --> 01:14:39.183
MADAM Clerk.

01:14:40.653 --> 01:14:41.520
I have one in memoriam today.

01:14:41.520 --> 01:14:42.221
I'm asking that we adjourn our

01:14:42.221 --> 01:14:45.580
meeting in memory of alan

01:14:45.580 --> 01:14:45.659
jacobs, our city's former

01:14:45.659 --> 01:14:48.590
